    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d112">

                <pb facs="0306" n="296" xml:id="pg296"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 15.</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Hammond to Mr. Elliot.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Foreign Office,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-02-05"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 5, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I am directed by Earl Russell to transmit
                    to you, to be laid before the Duke of Newcastle, the accompanying copy of a
                    letter from Messrs. Sinclair, Hamilton &amp; Co., stating their reasons for
                    believing Penguin island to be British territory; and I am to request that you
                    will move his grace to inform Lord Russell what answer should be returned to
                    Messrs. Sinclair, Hamilton &amp; Co.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>E. HAMMOND.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
